{
 "_about": [
  "The Purchase Orders prototype's data. Every organisation, supplier, product and order here is invented.",
  "Times are AGES, not dates (minutesAgo / daysAgo), resolved against the moment the page opens,",
  "so the list always opens on \"today\". js/data/resolve.js turns them into records.",
  "  products        the store's catalogue: units (secondary-base), price per secondary unit, GST, stock",
  "  rawMaterials    inputs the store buys but does not sell: in its MASTER and RAW-MATERIAL catalogues only",
  "  suppliers       external suppliers (sup-09 is a DEPARTMENT source: hidden from this screen)",
  "  locations       other locations of this organisation the store can buy from (internal sources)",
  "  purchaseOrders  one per row; `received` marks a delivered order's goods-received audit",
  "  customers       the organisations the store sells to, each in one customer-type catalogue",
  "  salesOrders     this store's own sales (to `customers`), which the purchase forecast reads as demand",
  "  catalogue       what each location sells: the store's own catalogue (every product), and the two",
  "                  internal locations' catalogues — their own product records, matched to the store's",
  "                  by article number, at their own base price and stock: { product: [price, stock] }",
  "  customerCatalogues  the store's customer-type catalogues besides DEFAULT: { name: [products] }",
  "  policies        guarantee / warranty templates the store attaches to products (a product's `policy`)"
 ],
